'''''What If...?''''' is an American animated [[anthology television series]] created by [[A. C. Bradley (screenwriter)|A. C. Bradley]] for the streaming service [[Disney+]], based on the [[Marvel Comics]] series [[What If (comics)|of the same name]]. It is [[List of Marvel Cinematic Universe television series (Marvel Studios)|the fourth television series]] in the [[Marvel Cinematic Universe]] (MCU) from [[Marvel Studios]], the first animated series from the studio, and the first series produced by [[Marvel Studios Animation]]. The series explores [[Alternate history|alternate timelines]] in the [[Multiverse (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|multiverse]] that show what would happen if major moments from [[List of Marvel Cinematic Universe films|the MCU films]] occurred differently. Bradley served as [[head writer]] for the first two seasons, with [[Matthew Chauncey]] taking over for the [[What If...? season 3|third]], and [[Bryan Andrews (filmmaker)|Bryan Andrews]] as the lead director.

[[Jeffrey Wright]] stars as the [[Watcher (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Watcher]], who narrates the series, alongside many MCU film actors reprising their roles. Marvel Studios was developing the series for Disney+ by the end of 2018, with Bradley and Andrews on board. It was officially announced in April 2019. Marvel Studios' head of visual development Ryan Meinerding helped define the series' [[cel-shaded]] animation style, which was designed to reflect the films and take inspiration from classic American illustrators. Animation for the series was provided by [[Flying Bark Productions]] and Stellar Creative Lab, with Blue Spirit and Squeeze also working on the [[What If...? season 1|first season]] and SDFX Studios working on the [[What If...? season 2|second]]. [[Stephan Franck]] was head of animation for the first season and a director on the second and third seasons, with Scott Wright as head of animation for the second and third seasons. Chauncey was the series' story editor before replacing Bradley as head writer.

The first season of ''What If...?'' premiered on August 11, 2021, and ran for nine episodes until October 6, as part of [[Marvel Cinematic Universe: Phase Four|Phase Four]] of the MCU. The second season was released daily from December 22 to 30, 2023, and the third and final season premiered on December 22, 2024, also released daily; both are part of [[Marvel Cinematic Universe: Phase Five|Phase Five]]. The series has received generally positive reviews, with praise for the voice acting, animation, creative storylines, and scenarios, although the episodes' length and writing received some criticism. An interactive [[Augmented reality|augmented]] and [[virtual reality]] story for the [[Apple Vision Pro]] headset, ''What If...? – An Immersive Story'', was released in May 2024, and a spin-off series titled ''[[Marvel Zombies (TV series)|Marvel Zombies]]'' premiered in September 2025. Three additional ''Zombies'' specials are scheduled for release yearly in 2027, 2028, and 2029.

== Premise ==
Following the establishment of the [[Multiverse (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|multiverse]] in the [[For All Time. Always.|first-season finale]] of ''[[Loki (TV series)|Loki]]'', ''What If...?'' explores various alternate timelines across the multiverse in which major moments from the [[List of Marvel Cinematic Universe films|Marvel Cinematic Universe (MCU) films]] occur differently, as observed by the [[Watcher (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Watcher]].<ref name="MarvelDisneyInvestorDay" /><ref name="DeadlinePressDay" /> In the [[What If...? season 2|second season]], following the formation of the [[Guardians of the Multiverse]], the Watcher continues to explore more strange worlds, meeting new heroes and keeping the multiverse safe.<ref name="Disney+DayDeadline" />

